A ring of sustain ability usually is not seen as an extremely good one.
It's nice if you don't have poison resistance and are trying to get it,
or to protect you from having your brain sucked out by a mind flayer,
but you shouldn't really eat it, as it will also prevent you from making
your stats *better*. And if you've maxed out all your stats, then you
don't really need it anymore.

Rings that are eaten by some players are e.g. increase damage, or 
intrinsics they don't already have.

You may eat metallic stuff (not all rings are metallic!) if you're 
polymorphed into a rust monster or a rock mole (?). Gelatinous cubes may
eat organic materiel like wooden rings.

The randomized structure of NetHack means that in some games all the good
rings will be non-eatable, in others you may be able to eat some of them.
Generally it's not necessary.

